waiver: harness-limit
reason: an aborting program is observable as an exit code on the
  interpreter and the native backends, which all print the same cause
  line and exit 134. The wasm leg builds with PrintMainResult and
  recovers the exit code from a trailing stdout line, which a trapping
  program never reaches: the runner sees empty stdout and a trap, not
  134. internal/testing/e2e/array_bounds_test.go covers the wasm trap.
